      "fetched_at": "2026-09-09T01:23:16.076Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "2048880815237685490",
      "url": "https://x.com/kunchenguid/status/2048880815237685490",
      "creator": "kunchenguid",
      "author": {
        "screen_name": "kunchenguid",
        "name": "Kun Chen",
        "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1946076752024895489/ScNir1Fy_200x200.jpg"
      },
      "reposted_by": null,
      "created_at": "2026-04-27T21:43:47.000Z",
      "sort_at": "2026-04-27T21:43:47.000Z",
      "text": "i tried https://gethandle.ai/ myself and it's legit one of the best tools for UX refinement\n\ninstead of writing giant prompts describing what you want to change and still not getting what you need, you change the UI in place and let the agent figure out how to make it happen",
      "media": [],
      "quote": {
        "id": "2048867664668537155",
        "url": "https://x.com/derekcheng/status/2048867664668537155",
        "author": {
          "screen_name": "derekcheng",
          "name": "Derek Cheng",
          "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1884724236302123008/zrhik4RK_200x200.jpg"
        },
        "created_at": "2026-04-27T20:51:32.000Z",
        "text": "Coding agents are great for first drafts of UI, but clumsy and slow when it comes to refining details.\n\nThe solution is to combine both: explore with an agent, but then be able to select a component, make direct edits and round-trip the changes back to code.\n\nEverything's done directly in the live product so there's no gap between design and reality.",
        "media": [
          {
            "id": "2048866901481402368",
            "type": "video",
            "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2048866901481402368/vid/avc1/1944x1080/9VBwMaX3VmElh0Ua.mp4?tag=21",
            "thumbnail_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2048866901481402368/img/fZOhWhex3AordTn3.jpg",
            "width": 1944,
            "height": 1080,
            "duration": 20.933
          }
        ]
      },
      "reply_to_id": null,
      "thread_root_id": "2048880815237685490",
